course: dictionary
lesson: 13166
title: Fossilisation: how remains become stone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fossilisation is the very slow process that turns the remains of a living thing into a fossil. It usually happens in rock, and it can take thousands or millions of years. «The process of fossilisation began when the animal was buried in mud.»
explain: Scientists explain fossilisation step by step. An animal dies, and it is buried quickly in mud or sand. The soft parts rot away. Then minerals slowly replace the bones, and layers of rock press down on top. «Layers of rock pressed down and turned the mud into stone.»
explain: Fossilisation can also describe ideas, habits or languages. When they stop changing and become fixed, we call that fossilisation too. «The club's rules had reached fossilisation, so nobody dared to change them.» Here the word means something has become frozen in place.
fact: Fossilisation is the slow process that turns remains or traces of a living thing into a fossil.
fact: Fossilisation usually happens in rock, and it can take thousands or millions of years.
fact: «Conditions for fossilisation» means the right conditions, such as quick burial in mud or sand.
fact: Mary Anning found famous fossils in Lyme Regis, a town on the coast of England.
fact: Figurative fossilisation means an idea, habit or language stops changing and becomes fixed.
exercise: «Fossilisation takes thousands or millions of years.» How long can fossilisation take? | *Thousands or millions of years | A few minutes | One single afternoon | One week
exercise: Fossilisation usually happens in which material? | Sugar | *Rock | Feathers | Air
exercise: «Her idea had reached fossilisation, so it never changed.» What does fossilisation mean here? | Ideas were dug up from the ground | Ideas were lost in the mud | Ideas grew very fast | *Ideas stopped changing and became fixed
test: In fossilisation, what slowly replaces the bones? | Leaves | *Minerals | Sunlight | Water only
test: Where are fossils usually found, according to the lesson? | Inside a cloud | *In rock | On the surface of the sea | In a glass jar
exam: Which step comes first in fossilisation? | *An animal dies | Layers of rock press down | The fossil is found by scientists | Minerals replace the bones
